<html><body style="font-family:sans-serif">
<p>Compliance Team, Factory Management, Legal:</p>

<p>Adidas Group's Social & Environmental Affairs (SEA) division has completed its <b>unannounced factory audit</b> at your Hangzhou manufacturing facility. The audit found <b style="color:#e00">four critical violations</b> requiring immediate remediation and a <b>Compliance Improvement Fund</b> contribution.</p>

<h3>一、Audit Summary</h3>
<table cellpadding=6 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5;width:200px">Audit Reference</td><td><b>SEA-2026-HZ-8842</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Factory</td><td>Your Company Manufacturing Facility (Hangzhou)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Audit Type</td><td>Unannounced (fourth audit this year)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Audit Date</td><td>October 24-25, 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Auditors</td><td>Sarah Chen (SEA Lead), Mike Wong (Environmental)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Workers Interviewed</td><td>47 (randomly selected across 3 shifts)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Overall Rating</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>C — FAIL (production suspension risk)</b></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>二、Critical Findings</h3>

<p><b>Finding 1 — Excessive Overtime (CRITICAL)</b></p>
<table cellpadding=5 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr style="background:#f0f0f0"><th>Indicator</th><th>Adidas Standard</th><th>Your Factory</th></tr>
<tr><td>Weekly overtime</td><td>Max 12 hours</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>28-35 hours</b></td></tr>
<tr><td>Monthly overtime</td><td>Max 36 hours</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>112 hours</b></td></tr>
<tr><td>Consecutive work days</td><td>Max 6 days</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>18 days</b></td></tr>
<tr><td>Workers affected</td><td>—</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>312 out of 847</b></td></tr>
</table>

<p><b>Finding 2 — Wage Violations (CRITICAL)</b></p>
<ul>
<li>142 workers paid below local minimum wage (Hangzhou: ¥2,480/month, actual: ¥2,150-2,320)</li>
<li>Overtime premium not paid at 1.5x/2x/3x rates (paid at flat 1.2x)</li>
<li>3 months of delayed social insurance contributions (July-September)</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Finding 3 — Safety Violations (HIGH)</b></p>
<ul>
<li>12 of 48 fire extinguishers past inspection date (expired 2025-Q4)</li>
<li>Emergency exit blocked by inventory on Floor 3</li>
<li>2 workers without proper PPE in chemical handling zone</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Finding 4 — Environmental Non-Compliance (HIGH)</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Wastewater discharge exceeding permitted zinc levels by 340%</li>
<li>Hazardous waste storage without secondary containment</li>
</ul>

<h3>三、Compliance Improvement Fund</h3>
<p>Per the Adidas Supplier Code of Conduct (Section 7.4), suppliers with a "C" rating must contribute to the <b>Compliance Improvement Fund</b>:</p>

<table cellpadding=5 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr style="background:#f0f0f0"><th>Item</th><th>Amount (USD)</th></tr>
<tr><td>Overtime compensation (312 workers × 3 months × average $180)</td><td>$168,480</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wage arrears (142 workers × 3 months × average $95)</td><td>$40,470</td></tr>
<tr><td>Social insurance back-payment</td><td>$68,200</td></tr>
<tr><td>Safety improvements (fire equipment, PPE, exit clearance)</td><td>$28,500</td></tr>
<tr><td>Environmental remediation (wastewater treatment)</td><td>$85,000</td></tr>
<tr><td>Worker welfare programme (mandatory for C-rated suppliers)</td><td>$32,000</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2" style="text-align:right"><b>Total: $422,650 USD</b></td></tr>
</table>

